Spon <christoph.blau@gmail.com> wrote:

> The easiest way I can think of to
> avoid this is to intersperse it with something that exercises
> wisdom, e.g. instead of 100s, type 19s, write ElberethElbereth
> in the dust, and repeat 5 times for the same time- lapse effect
> without the risk of wis loss (n19s if you're using number_pad).

Better only write Elbereth, as wisdom is only exercised when
the whole resulting engraving is meant to become a single,
case-sensitive and unadorned Elbereth. Even adding another
Elbereth to an existing one does not exercise wisdom.

Furthermore, not acquiring the habit to engrave a multiple
Elbereth in one step might save you from a hit while engraving.

-- Ralf


